Equivalence Groups Found
└── cooperative concurrency monkey-patching for async I/O (used with socketio)
    ├── Candidates : eventlet, gevent
    ├── Used APIs  : monkey_patch
    ├── Pitfalls   : API differs: eventlet.monkey_patch() vs gevent.monkey.patch_all() - not a
    │   literal 1:1 import swap; Flask-SocketIO requires specifying async_mode='gevent' or 
    │   configuring accordingly when switching from eventlet; Behavioral differences in DNS 
    │   resolution, subprocess handling, and threading patches between eventlet and gevent; 
    │   Must patch before importing any other modules that use the patched stdlib features 
    │   (ordering matters for both)
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── eventlet.monkey_patch() patches the standard library for cooperative green-thread 
        concurrency, which is required before Flask-SocketIO/socketio.run() operates in async 
        mode. gevent provides an equivalent monkey-patching mechanism 
        (gevent.monkey.patch_all()) and is a commonly supported alternative async mode for 
        Flask-SocketIO, making it a genuine drop-in substitute for this specific use case.

