    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses pycryptodome's Crypto.Cipher.AES module to perform AES-128-CBC 
        encryption/decryption with a fixed IV. pycryptodomex is the same library under the 
        'Cryptodome' namespace (avoids the historic PyCrypto/pycryptodome namespace collision)
        and exposes an essentially identical AES.new/.encrypt/.decrypt API, making it a near 
        drop-in replacement. cryptography's hazmat primitives (Cipher, algorithms.AES, 
        modes.CBC) can perform the same AES-CBC operation but with a materially different 
        object-oriented API (encryptor()/update()/finalize() instead of new()/encrypt()), so 
