    │   error_if_exists=) with Get/Put/Delete (capitalized); plyvel uses plyvel.DB(path, 
    │   create_if_missing=) with lowercase get/put/delete; lmdb requires explicit map_size and
    │   transaction (env.begin()) semantics, not a direct drop-in for simple get/put calls; 
    │   rocksdb (python-rocksdb) has its own Options/DB class API distinct from leveldb 
    │   bindings; leveldb's Get(key, default=False) trick for existence checking won't work 
    │   identically in other bindings (e.g., plyvel raises KeyError or returns None instead); 
    │   byte/bytearray return type conversions may differ between bindings
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file wraps the 'leveldb' Python binding to implement a BaseDB interface 
        (get/set/exists/delete) backed by an embedded on-disk key-value store. plyvel, lmdb, 
