    ├── Used APIs  : load, SafeLoader
    ├── Pitfalls   : ruamel.yaml's round-trip loader preserves comments/formatting which 
    │   PyYAML/oyaml do not — only relevant if the file re-serializes YAML, not the case here 
    │   since only load() is used; strictyaml was suggested but enforces strict typed schemas 
    │   and a different loading API (not a simple load()/Loader parameter), so it does not fit
    │   this usage pattern; Ensure consistent import path (ruamel.yaml vs ruamel_yaml) across 
    │   environments since 'ruamel' alone is often not directly importable in newer packaging
    └── The code uses ruamel.yaml.load(..., Loader=SafeLoader), which mirrors PyYAML's 
        yaml.load(stream, Loader=yaml.SafeLoader) API closely. oyaml is a thin wrapper around 
        PyYAML preserving dict ordering and exposes the same load()/SafeLoader interface, 
        making both genuine drop-in substitutes for this simple load-only usage.

