Equivalence Groups Found
└── YAML serialization for rendering config/output as YAML text
    ├── Candidates : ruamel.yaml, PyYAML, oyaml
    ├── Used APIs  : yaml.safe_dump
    ├── Pitfalls   : ruamel.yaml (newer API) deprecates safe_dump in favor of YAML().dump with
    │   rt/safe modes in later versions — pinning to the legacy API surface is needed for a 
    │   clean swap; PyYAML's safe_dump has slightly different default formatting (line width, 
    │   key ordering) which could change rendered template output; ruamel preserves 
    │   comments/formatting on round-trip which PyYAML does not, though this file only uses 
    │   one-way dumping so it's not exercised here
    └── ruamel.yaml's safe_dump is used as a jinja2 filter to serialize data to YAML. PyYAML 
        exposes an identical yaml.safe_dump function signature, making it a near drop-in 
        replacement, and oyaml is a thin wrapper around PyYAML with the same API that 
        preserves dict ordering.

